5. User Flow Explanation

The user opens the Student Task Planner website.

The user enters the task title, subject and due date.

The user clicks the Add Task button.

The application validates the entered information.

If the information is valid, the task is saved.

The task is displayed in the task list.

The user can edit, complete or delete a task.

6. Expected Result

The wireframe provides a clear visual representation of the Student Task Planner website. The user flow explains the complete interaction between the user and the application.

7. Conclusion

The wireframe and user flow help in planning the website before development. They make the design and functionality easier to understand and implement.